check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8489148Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8499065Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8605309Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8615703Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8616702Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8617682Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8618206Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8618692Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8619769Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8620421Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8620873Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8621695Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8622108Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8622945Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8623830Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8624451Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8624933Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8625314Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8625541Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8625891Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8626152Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8626949Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8627107Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8627221Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8627405Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8627721Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8628254Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8629481Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8629703Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8629903Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8630096Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8630651Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8631474Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8632076Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8632414Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8632718Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8633150Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8633594Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8646515Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8647328Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8658710Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8659386Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8659889Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8660862Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8661528Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8680606Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8681126Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:47.8691839Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
