check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2141356Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2148896Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2240410Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2249098Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2249680Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2250415Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2250700Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2250942Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2251656Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2251993Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2252221Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2253126Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2253509Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2253975Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2254610Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2255908Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2256366Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2256586Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2256850Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2257181Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2257444Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2257898Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2258060Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2258236Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2258468Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2258855Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2259503Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2259830Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2260009Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2260230Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2260571Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2261109Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2261629Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2262165Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2262543Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2262905Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2263361Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2263856Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2274282Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2275331Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2284183Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2285011Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2287328Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2287861Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2288368Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2302994Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2304003Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2312124Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2312699Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2313275Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2313576Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2313763Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T03:43:49.2314049Z 
